"""Public-facing introduction to the twelve approved school-concept features."""
from html import escape

CHAPTERS = [
    ('Open a world of possibility.', 'Begin with discovery', [
        ('Performing & creative arts', 'Give talent a stage.', 'Imagine a student discovering the drums, finding a voice in choir, then stepping into a musical. Instruments, acting, dance, visual arts and production give young people many ways to discover what they can bring to the world.'),
        ('Practical & creative technology', 'Make the future something they build.', 'A robot that moves. A game they programmed. A film or 3D model that began as an idea. Students learn to direct AI agents, evaluate the results and use powerful tools ethically. Technology becomes a medium for their own creativity.'),
        ('Friendships, ability & attention', 'Let them belong. Help them grow.', 'Build a school where friendships and individual progress both matter. Class placement considers age and social fit; academic work follows ability. Small classes and specialist teachers make room to notice a strength, work through a difficulty and encourage the next step.')
    ]),
    ('Give that possibility roots.', 'From discovery to direction', [
        ('Arts, Technology & Double Majors', 'Let a passion become a path.', 'The performer. The inventor. The student who lights up at both. Arts, Technology and Double Major options give those interests a place in the school week, with time to practice, create and take them seriously.'),
        ('Christian & nondenominational', 'Put Christ at the heart.', 'Worship, chapel, Bible teaching and Christian studies belong in the life of the school. Welcome believers from different denominations, while leaving denominational questions with families and their churches. Faith gives learning a deeper purpose: using our gifts to honor God and serve others.'),
        ('Subjects offered year after year', 'Build depth that a short course cannot.', 'Imagine what years of Spanish, music or filmmaking could make possible. Subjects return year after year, giving students time to move beyond a first taste, develop their craft and take on more ambitious work as their ability grows.')
    ]),
    ('Turn “I could” into “I will.”', 'From ability to initiative', [
        ('Leadership & entrepreneurship', 'Make room for their moonshot.', 'A student farmers market turns an idea into something people can buy. Debate gives convictions a voice. Leadership and business projects give students practice in taking responsibility, solving problems and pursuing ambitious ideas that could benefit their community.'),
        ('School currency & prize challenges', 'Give effort something to aim for.', 'A robotics challenge. A filmmaking competition. A prize worth working toward. School currency recognizes everyday effort and contribution, while creative and technical challenges can offer real-money rewards. River Tech’s Gold (RTC) makes progress and participation part of school life.'),
        ('Culture & character', 'Raise people others can count on.', 'Talent matters. So does the person carrying it. Responsibility, Integrity, Voice, Excellence and Respect—the RIVER values—shape clear expectations and calm correction. A conservative Christian culture makes room for patriotism, hard work, earned achievement, grit and the courage to put things right.')
    ]),
    ('Prepare them for a life that matters.', 'From school to the wider world', [
        ('Whole-person education', 'Keep life bigger than a screen.', 'God, family, church, community and the outdoors belong alongside technical skill. Relationships, money, health and everyday responsibility are part of learning, with device-free time for lunch, recess and physical activity. Build capable people who know there is a world worth stepping into.'),
        ('Trips, celebrations & families', 'Become a place a community loves.', 'Take learning beyond the building through field trips. Bring families together for celebrations and shared events. Invite parents to contribute their time, ideas and experience. A school can become a place of shared memories, friendships and belonging.'),
        ('Annual essays & college coaching', 'Help the next chapter begin here.', 'Each year, high-school students tackle a substantial essay, building the thinking and writing experience they will need beyond school. Online college courses, taken during class time with teacher support, offer a practical way to begin that next chapter while still surrounded by familiar encouragement.')
    ])
]

